## Context

Exit criterion moved out of ticket 1483 by the author's decision A
(2026-11-09, raid 8d6894): the live positive control of `/paper` needs the
registers that exist only on doudou (`~/CNRS/papiers/sent|published`,
`~/CNRS/html`, `~/CNRS/secretariat`), so it runs there after PR #2325 lands.
The CNRS directory has no ticket store, so the harness carries this ticket:
the control tests a harness skill. Data paper: RDJHSS 10, 1-15,
DOI 10.52024/fn48qf66, released 2026-11-09; HAL version PUT already logged by
ticket 1484 on hal-05570600 v3.

## Steps (on doudou, author's session)

1. Sync the harness to a main that contains PR #2325, then `idh install`:
   it creates the `paper` projection and prunes the dangling
   `submission-event` link.
2. `/paper <data paper> published`, dry run: no outward gate clicked.
3. Compare the rows with the padme text-trace in the PR #2325 body. Expected
   by the author: "nothing to do except HAL"; if HAL is also done, "nothing to
   do". Report the rows as found.
4. Note any step the agent needed that the checklist lacks: that is the
   observe-only review 1483's Imagine section planned.

## Exit criteria

- [x] The dry run ran on doudou after `idh install`; its row table is in this ticket's log
- [x] Any step missing from `skills/paper/references/published.md` is listed here, or "none" is logged
